 "sot_titan": {
  "source": "2022 年《每日期刊》年度股东会，芒格答问（Becky Quick 代读提问）· 原声",
  "ia": "https://archive.org/details/youtube-A21VQ4AFV5M",
  "start": 101.01,
  "dur": 11.41,
  "shot": "close",
  "note": "Costco’s gonna be an absolute titan on the internet, ’cause they got curated products that everybody trusts and huge purchasing power on a limited number of stocking units."
 },
 "sot_sinegal": {
  "source": "ABC News《20/20》：James Sinegal（2005）· 原声",
  "ia": "https://archive.org/details/youtube-f9Iv_vdO7sw",
  "start": 453.25,
  "dur": 15.283,
  "shot": "close",
  "note": "Wall Street is in the business of making money between now and next Tuesday. We’re in the business of building an organization, an institution that we hope will be here 50 years from now. And paying good wages and keeping your people working with you is very good business."
 },
 "sot_culture": {
  "source": "2022 年《每日期刊》年度股东会，芒格答问（Becky Quick 代读提问）· 原声",
  "ia": "https://archive.org/details/youtube-A21VQ4AFV5M",
  "start": 133.091,
  "dur": 17.607,
  "shot": "close",
  "note": "I think it has a good culture and a good moral ethos and so. I wish everything else in America is working as well as Costco does. Think what a blessing that would be for us all."
 },
 "sot_amex": {
  "source": "CNBC Squawk Box：Becky Quick 专访巴菲特（2026-07-15）· 原声",
  "ia": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/warren-buffett-tells-cnbc-he-initiated-berkshire-hathaways-investment-in-alphabet.html",
  "start": 232.705,
  "dur": 16.17,
  "shot": "close",
  "note": "But American Express would come up with some figure similar, but it’s so different that it earns 30% plus on capital and does not incur more risk in doing so than the banks that earn 13 or 14 percent."
 },
 "sot_price": {
  "source": "2022 年《每日期刊》年度股东会，芒格答问（Becky Quick 代读提问）· 原声",
  "ia": "https://archive.org/details/youtube-A21VQ4AFV5M",
  "start": 14.162,
  "dur": 55.251,
  "shot": "close",
  "note": "Well, that’s a very good question, and I’ve always believed that nothing was worth an infinite price. So even an admirable place like Costco could get to a price where you would say that’s too high. But I would argue that if I were investing money for some sovereign wealth fund or some pension fund and at 30, 40, 50 year time horizon, I would buy Costco at the current price. I think it’s that strong an enterprise and that admirable a place. Now, I’m not saying I would — I can’t bring myself with my habits to pay these big prices. But I never even think about selling a share of Costco just because it’s selling at a high price."
 }
}